        </if>
      </else>
    </if>

    <if>
      <condition auto:"FAILED" type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          system      : "SunOS"
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "ClientAliveInterval"
          file        : "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"
          regex       : "(?i)^[\\s]*ClientAliveInterval[\\s]+"
          expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*ClientAliveInterval[\\s]+[\"]?600+[\"]?[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>

        <custom_item>
          system      : "SunOS"
          type        : FILE_CONTENT_CHECK
          description : "ClientAliveCountMax"
          file        : "/etc/ssh/sshd_config"
          regex       : "(?i)^[\\s]*ClientAliveCountMax[\\s]+"
          expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*ClientAliveCountMax[\\s]+[\"]?0+[\"]?[\\s]*$"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <report type:"PASSED">
          description : "1.136 SOL-11.1-050460"
          info        : "The operating system must terminate all sessions and network connections when nonlocal maintenance is completed.

GROUP ID: V-216162RULE ID: SV-216162r986457

Nonlocal maintenance and diagnostic activities are those activities conducted by individuals communicating through a network, either an external network (e.g., the internet) or an internal network.

The operating system needs to ensure all sessions and network connections are terminated when nonlocal maintenance is completed."
          solution    : "The root role is required.

Configure the system to disconnect SSH sessions after 10 minutes of inactivity.

pfedit /etc/ssh/sshd_config

Insert the two lines:

ClientAliveInterval 600ClientAliveCountMax 0

Restart the SSH service with the new configuration.

svcadm restart svc:/network/ssh"
          reference   : "800-171|3.13.9,800-171r3|03.13.09,800-53|SC-10,800-53r5|SC-10,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-001133,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.20,ITSG-33|SC-10,ITSG-33|SC-10a.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T2.3.8,NESA|T4.5.1,NESA|T5.5.1,Rule-ID|SV-216162r986457_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-050460,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.6,Vuln-ID|V-216162"
          see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
          show_output : YES
        </report>
      </then>
    </if>

    <custom_item>
      system      : "SunOS"
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.137 SOL-11.1-050470"
      info        : "The operating system must prevent internal users from sending out packets which attempt to manipulate or spoof invalid IP addresses.

GROUP ID: V-216163RULE ID: SV-216163r959010

Manipulation of IP addresses can allow untrusted systems to appear as trusted hosts, bypassing firewall and other security mechanism and resulting in system penetration."
      solution    : "Determine the name of the zone that you are currently securing.

zonename

If the command output is \"global\", then only the \"phys\" and \"SR-IOV\" interfaces assigned to the global zone require configuration. If using a non-Global zone, then all \"phys\" and \"SR-IOV\" interfaces assigned to the zone require configuration.

The Network Link Security profile is required.

Determine which network interfaces are available and what protection modes are enabled and required.

Enable link protection based on each configured network interface type.

For InfiniBand:pfexec dladm set-linkprop -p protection=restricted,ip-nospoof,dhcp-nospoof [interface name]

For IP forwarding:pfexec dladm set-linkprop -p protection=mac-nospoof,restricted,dhcp-nospoof [interface name]

For SR-IOV:pfexec dladm set-linkprop -p protection=mac-nospoof,restricted,dhcp-nospoof [interface name]

For Ethernet without IP forwarding:pfexec dladm set-linkprop -p protection=mac-nospoof,restricted,ip-nospoof,dhcp-nospoof [interface name]"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216163r959010_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-050470,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216163"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
      cmd         : "#!/bin/bash

    overall_status=0
    checked_interfaces=0
    my_zone=$(zonename)

    interfaces=$(/usr/sbin/dladm show-link -Z  | /usr/xpg4/bin/awk -v zone=\"$my_zone\" '$2 == zone && ($3 == \"phys\" || $3 == \"sriov\") {print $1}')

    if [ -z \"$interfaces\" ]; then
      /usr/bin/echo \"No physical or SR-IOV interfaces found in the current zone ($my_zone). Check is Not Applicable.\"
      exit 0
    fi


    for link in $interfaces; do
      checked_interfaces=$((checked_interfaces + 1))
      link_passed=1

      current_protection=$(/usr/sbin/dladm show-linkprop -p protection -o value \"$link\")
      media_type=$(/usr/sbin/dladm show-phys -p -o media \"$link\")
      ip_forwarding_v4=$(/usr/sbin/ipadm show-ifprop -c -p forwarding -o current -m ipv4 \"$link\" 2>/dev/null)
      ip_forwarding_v6=$(/usr/sbin/ipadm show-ifprop -c -p forwarding -o current -m ipv6 \"$link\" 2>/dev/null)
      is_forwarding=0
      if [[ \"$ip_forwarding_v4\" == \"on\" || \"$ip_forwarding_v6\" == \"on\" ]]; then
        is_forwarding=1
        /usr/bin/echo \"IP Forwarding is ON for $link\"
      else
        /usr/bin/echo \"IP Forwarding is OFF for $link\"
      fi

      required_protections=\"\"
      if [[ \"$media_type\" == \"Infiniband\" ]]; then
        required_protections=\"restricted ip-nospoof dhcp-nospoof\"
      elif [[ $is_forwarding -eq 1 ]]; then
        required_protections=\"mac-nospoof restricted dhcp-nospoof\"
      else
        required_protections=\"mac-nospoof restricted ip-nospoof dhcp-nospoof\"
      fi

      for prop in $required_protections; do
        if ! /usr/bin/echo \"$current_protection\" | grep -q \"$prop\"; then
          /usr/bin/echo \"Interface '$link' ($media_type) *is missing* required protection: '$prop'\"
          link_passed=0
          overall_status=1
        else
          /usr/bin/echo \"Interface '$link' ($media_type) has required protection: '$prop'\"
        fi
      done

      if [ $link_passed -eq 1 ]; then
        /usr/bin/echo \"Interface '$link' ($media_type) has all required protections.\"
      fi
    done

        # Final result
    if [ $checked_interfaces -eq 0 ]; then
        /usr/bin/echo \"WARNING: No interfaces were checked. This may indicate a script error.\"
    elif [ $overall_status -eq 0 ]; then
        /usr/bin/echo \"All checked interfaces ($checked_interfaces) are compliant.\"
        /usr/bin/echo \"PASS\"
    else
        /usr/bin/echo \"One or more interfaces are not compliant.\"
        /usr/bin/echo \"FAIL\";
    fi"
      expect      : "^PASS$"
    </custom_item>

    <if>
      <condition type:"AND">
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "Global zone auditing is configured."
          cmd         : "/usr/bin/zonename"
          expect      : "^global$"
        </custom_item>
      </condition>

      <then>
        <custom_item>
          type        : CMD_EXEC
          description : "1.138 SOL-11.1-050480"
          info        : "Wireless network adapters must be disabled.

GROUP ID: V-216164RULE ID: SV-216164r958358

The use of wireless networking can introduce many different attack vectors into the organization's network. Common attack vectors such as malicious association and ad hoc networks will allow an attacker to spoof a wireless access point (AP), allowing validated systems to connect to the malicious AP and enabling the attacker to monitor and record network traffic. These malicious APs can also serve to create a man-in-the-middle attack or be used to create a denial-of-service to valid network resources."
          solution    : "Configure the system to disable all wireless network interfaces."
