    </if>

    <custom_item>
      system      : "SunOS"
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.182 SOL-11.1-080040"
      info        : "Process core dumps must be disabled unless needed.

GROUP ID: V-216208RULE ID: SV-216208r959010

Process core dumps contain the memory in use by the process when it crashed. Process core dump files can be of significant size and their use can result in file systems filling to capacity, which may result in denial of service. Process core dumps can be useful for software debugging."
      solution    : "The Maintenance and Repair profile is required.

Change the process core dump configuration to disable core dumps globally and on a per process basis.

coreadm -d globalcoreadm -d processcoreadm -d global-setidcoreadm -d proc-setidcoreadm -e log"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216208r959010_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-080040,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216208"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/coreadm | /usr/bin/grep enabled | /usr/bin/grep -v logging | /bin/awk '{print} END {if (NR == 0) print \"pass\" ; else print \"fail\"}'"
      expect      : "^pass$"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      type        : CMD_EXEC
      description : "1.183 SOL-11.1-080045"
      info        : "The system must be configured to store any process core dumps in a specific, centralized directory.

GROUP ID: V-216209RULE ID: SV-216209r959010

Specifying a centralized location for core file creation allows for the centralized protection of core files. Process core dumps contain the memory in use by the process when it crashed. Any data the process was handling may be contained in the core file, and it must be protected accordingly. If process core dump creation is not configured to use a centralized directory, core dumps may be created in a directory that does not have appropriate ownership or permissions configured, which could result in unauthorized access to the core dumps."
      solution    : "The root role is required.

Set the core file directory and file pattern.

coreadm -g /var/share/cores/core.%f.%p"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216209r959010_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-080045,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216209"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
      cmd         : "/usr/bin/coreadm | /usr/xpg4/bin/grep 'global core file pattern'"
      expect      : "(?i)^[\\s]*global core file pattern:[\\s]*@CORE_DUMP_PATTERN@"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      system      : "SunOS"
      type        : FILE_CHECK
      description : "1.184 SOL-11.1-080050"
      info        : "The centralized process core dump data directory must be owned by root.

GROUP ID: V-216210RULE ID: SV-216210r959010

Process core dumps contain the memory in use by the process when it crashed. Any data the process was handling may be contained in the core file, and it must be protected accordingly. If the centralized process core dump data directory is not owned by root, the core dumps contained in the directory may be subject to unauthorized access."
      solution    : "The root role is required.

Change the owner of the core file directory.

chown root [core file directory]"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216210r959010_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-080050,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216210"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
      file        : "@CORE_FILE_DIR@"
      owner       : "root"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      system      : "SunOS"
      type        : FILE_CHECK
      description : "1.185 SOL-11.1-080060"
      info        : "The centralized process core dump data directory must be group-owned by root, bin, or sys.

GROUP ID: V-216211RULE ID: SV-216211r959010

Process core dumps contain the memory in use by the process when it crashed. Any data the process was handling may be contained in the core file, and it must be protected accordingly. If the centralized process core dump data directory is not group-owned by a system group, the core dumps contained in the directory may be subject to unauthorized access."
      solution    : "The root role is required.

Change the group-owner of the core file directory to root, bin or sys.

Example: chgrp root [core file directory]"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216211r959010_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-080060,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216211"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
      file        : "@CORE_FILE_DIR@"
      group       : "root" || "sys" || "bin"
    </custom_item>

    <custom_item>
      system      : "SunOS"
      type        : FILE_CHECK
      description : "1.186 SOL-11.1-080070"
      info        : "The centralized process core dump data directory must have mode 0700 or less permissive.

GROUP ID: V-216212RULE ID: SV-216212r959010

Process core dumps contain the memory in use by the process when it crashed. Any data the process was handling may be contained in the core file, and it must be protected accordingly. If the process core dump data directory has a mode more permissive than 0700, unauthorized users may be able to view or to modify sensitive information contained in any process core dumps in the directory."
      solution    : "The root role is required.

Change the mode of the core file directory.

chmod 0700 [core file directory]"
      reference   : "800-171|3.4.2,800-171r3|03.04.02a.,800-53|CM-6b.,800-53r5|CM-6b.,CAT|II,CCI|CCI-000366,CN-L3|8.1.10.6(d),CSF|PR.IP-1,CSF2.0|DE.CM-09,CSF2.0|PR.PS-01,GDPR|32.1.b,HIPAA|164.306(a)(1),ISO-27001-2022|A.8.9,ITSG-33|CM-6b.,LEVEL|2M,NESA|T3.2.1,Rule-ID|SV-216212r959010_rule,STIG-ID|SOL-11.1-080070,SWIFT-CSCv1|2.3,Vuln-ID|V-216212"
      see_also    : "https://workbench.cisecurity.org/benchmarks/23873"
      file        : "@CORE_FILE_DIR@"
      mask        : "7077"
    </custom_item>

